**New Evidence**
- `Expression of Gratitude on the Conclusion of Peace Talks` (PM Office, 2022-12-01)
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Expression of Gratitude on the Conclusion of Peace Talks","publisher":"FDRE Office of the Prime Minister","publication_date":"2022-12-01","url":"https://pmo.gov.et/press_release/","claim":"The PMO said the South Africa peace agreement would move Ethiopia forward on the reform path and reaffirmed commitment to peace and implementation.","locator":"Press Releases page, Dec. 1, 2022 item, lines 35-38","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary official statement by the PM office, strong for the fact of the commitment but self-serving on sincerity.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-period 2022; issued immediately after the peace talks.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Abiy office statement; shows his public commitment, but not independent proof of personal candor.","contrary_evidence":["Subsequent reporting still questioned full implementation and included continuing distrust around the ceasefire process."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.8","7B.10"]}

- `Ethiopia's Abiy vows 'honest' implementation of Tigray truce` (Reuters via Euronews, 2022-11-16)
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ethiopia's Abiy vows 'honest' implementation of Tigray truce","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-11-16","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/11/16/ethiopia-conflict","claim":"Abiy told parliament he would implement the ceasefire honestly and said the truce was needed so peace would be sustainable.","locator":"lines 660-665","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting on Abiy's own parliamentary remarks, with precise date and direct quotation context.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-period 2022, after the November ceasefire agreement.","ruler_attribution":"Direct ruler statement; supports public commitment and correction, but sincerity remains inferred.","contrary_evidence":["Other 2022 reporting described incomplete implementation and continued skepticism about the government's peace process."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.8","7B.10"]}

- `Gov't Establishes National Committee To Coordinate Anti-Corruption Campaign` (ENA, 2022-11-17)
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Gov't Establishes National Committee To Coordinate Anti-Corruption Campaign","publisher":"Ethiopian News Agency","publication_date":"2022-11-17","url":"https://www.ena.et/web/eng/w/en_40240","claim":"Abiy said the government created a national committee to coordinate an anti-corruption campaign, investigate officials and bribe givers/takers, and bring culprits before court.","locator":"lines 55-63 and 70-72","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official statement with specific anti-corruption actions, but it remains self-reported and not an independent audit.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"Direct statement of his anti-corruption posture; proves initiative, not effectiveness or personal non-corruption.","contrary_evidence":["Freedom House and other monitors still described weak transparency and corruption problems in the same period."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}

- `World Leaders Archive: Ethiopia` (CIA, 2022-08-24)
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"World Leaders Archive: Ethiopia","publisher":"Central Intelligence Agency","publication_date":"2022-08-24","url":"https://www.cia.gov/resources/world-leaders/historical-data/2022-september/ethiopia","claim":"The 2022 cabinet roster lists Abiy Ahmed as prime minister and Ahmed Shide as finance minister, among other cabinet members.","locator":"lines 21-31 and 54-64","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Authoritative roster for officeholders and dates, though it does not by itself establish merit or independence.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Target-period 2022 cabinet snapshot","ruler_attribution":"Anchors who Abiy appointed or retained in office; motive and anti-crony intent remain unproven.","contrary_evidence":["A roster alone does not show whether appointments were merit-based or politically loyalist."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.9"]}

- `Ahmed Shide` (World Bank Live, unknown date on page)
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ahmed Shide","publisher":"World Bank Live","publication_date":"unknown","url":"https://live.worldbank.org/en/experts/a/ahmed-shide","claim":"Ahmed Shide had served as Ethiopia's finance minister since 2018 and previously held several finance and transport posts; the profile also lists economics and development credentials.","locator":"line 46 and line 49","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Institutional biography with specific role history and qualifications; strong on competence, weak on ruler motive.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly relevant to the 2022 cabinet and its continuity.","ruler_attribution":"Supports the inference that Abiy retained a long-serving technocratic minister, but it does not rule out cronyism elsewhere.","contrary_evidence":["One technocratic appointment does not establish a generally merit-based or integrity-preserving cabinet."],"lenses":["7B.5"]}

- `Ethiopia: Freedom in the World 2022 Country Report` (Freedom House, 2022)
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ethiopia: Freedom in the World 2022 Country Report","publisher":"Freedom House","publication_date":"2022","url":"https://freedomhouse.org/country/ethiopia/freedom-world/2022","claim":"The report says authorities were opaque and at times dishonest about Eritrean forces in Tigray, and that journalists remained under pressure, imprisonment, and media restrictions.","locator":"lines 163-177","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent rights monitor with a detailed country report; the claims are broad but directly address transparency and press conditions.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Published in 2022; much of the text summarizes 2021 conditions that formed the 2022 baseline.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Abiy's governing party and state communications, but the report is broader than personal misconduct alone.","contrary_evidence":["The same report notes initial steps toward greater openness and some corruption arrests, so the picture is mixed at the institutional level."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}

- `World Report 2022: Ethiopia` (Human Rights Watch, 2022)
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"World Report 2022: Ethiopia","publisher":"Human Rights Watch","publication_date":"2022","url":"https://www.hrw.org/world-report/2022/country-chapters/ethiopia","claim":"HRW said government attacks and restrictions on media and free expression increased, with journalists and outspoken public figures intimidated, expelled, arrested, and Addis Standard suspended.","locator":"lines 111-116","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent monitoring report with specific examples and contemporaneous corroboration.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"2022 report, mostly reflecting late-2021 to early-2022 conditions that carried into the target year.","ruler_attribution":"This is state-action evidence under Abiy's government, but not proof of his personal command in each case.","contrary_evidence":["HRW also notes earlier liberalizing steps under Abiy, so the record is not one-directional."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}

- `Ethiopia arrests former government officials from Tigray, rights body says` (Reuters via Euronews, 2022-03-19)
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ethiopia arrests former government officials from Tigray, rights body says","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-03-19","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/03/19/us-ethiopia-conflict-arrests","claim":"Ethiopian authorities detained at least eight senior officials from Tigray, including members of the region's last administration, and the reasons for the arrests were unclear.","locator":"lines 664-678","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters report with specific date, agency statement, and clear attribution to Ethiopian authorities.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Abiy's government apparatus; personal direction is not shown, but the state nexus is strong.","contrary_evidence":["Officials did not comment and the stated reasons were unclear, so this is more evidence of coercive state practice than of personal concealment."],"lenses":["7B.7","7B.9","7B.10"]}

- `Ethiopian authorities arrest 11 employees of 4 independent media outlets` (CPJ, 2022-05-24)
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ethiopian authorities arrest 11 employees of 4 independent media outlets","publisher":"Committee to Protect Journalists","publication_date":"2022-05-24","url":"https://cpj.org/2022/05/ethiopian-authorities-arrest-11-employees-of-4-independent-media-outlets/","claim":"CPJ said Ethiopian authorities arrested at least 11 journalists and media workers in Amhara and Addis Ababa as part of a broader crackdown, and urged release without charge.","locator":"lines 516-526","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Specialist press-freedom monitor with detailed case-specific reporting and contemporaneous response.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact target-year 2022","ruler_attribution":"State repression under Abiy's government; direct personal order is not demonstrated, but continued tolerance after notice is plausible.","contrary_evidence":["Authorities described the operation as law enforcement and denied targeting journalism as such."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}

- `Ethiopia detains journalists Bekalu Alamrew and Meaza Mohammed in ongoing media crackdown` (CPJ, 2022-06-03)
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ethiopia detains journalists Bekalu Alamrew and Meaza Mohammed in ongoing media crackdown","publisher":"Committee to Protect Journalists","publication_date":"2022-06-03","url":"https://cpj.org/2022/06/ethiopia-detains-journalists-bekalu-alamrew-and-meaza-mohammed-in-ongoing-media-crackdown/","claim":"CPJ reported that police detained Bekalu Alamrew and Meaza Mohammed, charged them in vague terms, and that the court granted extended detention while no formal charges were filed.","locator":"lines 516-525","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Detailed alert from a specialist press-freedom organization with named detainees and court process details.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact target-year 2022","ruler_attribution":"Shows coercive treatment of critical journalists by Ethiopian authorities; direct personal involvement is not shown.","contrary_evidence":["Police and federal officials said the detainees were being handled as criminal cases rather than press cases."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}

- `Ethiopian authorities re-arrest journalist Yayesew Shimelis 1 week after release on bail` (CPJ, 2022-06-29)
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ethiopian authorities re-arrest journalist Yayesew Shimelis 1 week after release on bail","publisher":"Committee to Protect Journalists","publication_date":"2022-06-29","url":"https://cpj.org/2022/06/ethiopian-authorities-re-arrest-journalist-yayesew-shimelis-1-week-after-release-on-bail/","claim":"CPJ said Ethiopian security personnel re-arrested Yayesew Shimelis and warned that authorities were using the judicial system to punish journalists whose reporting did not align with the government's narrative.","locator":"lines 516-517","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Specific, contemporaneous, and directly tied to the treatment of a named journalist and the justice system.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact target-year 2022","ruler_attribution":"Supports a ruler-level pattern of retaliatory pressure on truth-tellers; the article does not prove Abiy personally ordered the arrest.","contrary_evidence":["Authorities did not publicly provide a substantive justification in the CPJ account."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}

- `Despite ban on meeting press, local CSOs call for immediate peace in Ethiopia, basic services provision in Tigray, other conflict-hit areas` (Addis Standard, 2022-09-07)
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Despite ban on meeting press, local CSOs call for immediate peace in Ethiopia, basic services provision in Tigray, other conflict hit areas","publisher":"Addis Standard","publication_date":"2022-09-07","url":"https://addisstandard.com/news-despite-ban-on-meeting-press-local-csos-call-for-immediate-peace-in-ethiopia-basic-services-provision-in-tigray-other-conflict-hit-areas/","claim":"Addis Standard reported that security forces blocked 35 local civil society organizations from meeting the media to issue a peace statement.","locator":"lead paragraph around line 70","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Local independent outlet with a concrete event, though the article relies on reported facts and does not itself prove central authorization.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact target-year 2022","ruler_attribution":"Security personnel blocking civil society media access is attributable to the governing environment, but the article does not isolate Abiy's personal order.","contrary_evidence":["The CSOs later issued their statement online, so the suppression was partial rather than total."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}

- `Two years of internet shutdowns: people in Tigray, Ethiopia, deserve better` (Access Now, 2022-11-04)
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Two years of internet shutdowns: people in Tigray, Ethiopia, deserve better","publisher":"Access Now","publication_date":"2022-11-04","url":"https://www.accessnow.org/press-release/two-years-internet-shutdowns-tigray/","claim":"Access Now said authorities had maintained an internet shutdown in Tigray for two years, preventing communication, access to information, and accountability over violence.","locator":"lines 242-250","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Digital-rights specialist reporting on a prolonged, well-documented shutdown with explicit accountability concerns.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact target-year 2022","ruler_attribution":"Strong state nexus under Abiy's government; it shows use of communication control, though not a personal enrichment case.","contrary_evidence":["Peace talks were underway by late 2022, so the shutdown sat alongside partial de-escalation rather than uninterrupted maximal conflict."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.8","7B.10"]}

- `Ethiopia launches a national dialogue, but divisions run deep` (The New Humanitarian, 2022-04-18)
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ethiopia launches a national dialogue, but divisions run deep","publisher":"The New Humanitarian","publication_date":"2022-04-18","url":"https://www.thenewhumanitarian.org/news-feature/2022/04/18/ethiopia-launches-national-dialogue-divisions-run-deep","claim":"The article said key rebel groups were excluded from the national dialogue, opposition figures accused the government of trying to orchestrate the process, and Abiy urged Ethiopians to participate.","locator":"lines 65-68 and 80-110","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Careful field reporting with named participants, direct quotes, and clear description of the dispute over inclusiveness.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"The dialogue design was Abiy-government driven; the exclusion is relevant to his leadership, though not a direct personal fraud finding.","contrary_evidence":["Commission officials said the process was inclusive and open, so there is genuine dispute over intent and design."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.6","7B.8","7B.10"]}

- `National Dialogue Commission, Civil Society Organizations Council Ink Partnership Agreement` (ENA, 2022-11-10)
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"National Dialogue Commission, Civil Society Organizations Council Ink Partnership Agreement","publisher":"Ethiopian News Agency","publication_date":"2022-11-10","url":"https://www.ena.et/web/eng/w/en_40007","claim":"The National Dialogue Commission and the Ethiopian Civil Society Organizations Council signed an agreement to work in partnership on the dialogue process.","locator":"lines 55-61","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct official event record, strong for the fact of the partnership but not for whether inclusion was substantively open.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact target-year 2022","ruler_attribution":"Shows a government-backed attempt to broaden participation, but not proof of a genuinely independent process.","contrary_evidence":["The earlier exclusion complaints and government-control concerns remained unresolved in parallel reporting."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.8","7B.10"]}

- `Disclosure and Registration of Assets Proclamation` (PolicyVault.Africa, current version January 2022)
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Disclosure and Registration of Assets Proclamation","publisher":"PolicyVault.Africa","publication_date":"January 2022","url":"https://policyvault.africa/policy/disclosure-and-registration-of-assets-proclamation/?version=0","claim":"The current January 2022 version says public-official asset disclosure and registration are crucial for transparent and accountable government and that public and private affairs should not intertwine.","locator":"search-result snippet / current version summary","source_type":"legal","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"Repository transcription of a formal proclamation; strong for the existence and wording of the rule, weaker for implementation or enforcement.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Institutional framework current in January 2022, not direct Abiy conduct.","ruler_attribution":"National legal context only; no evidence here that Abiy personally complied or benefited.","contrary_evidence":["No direct 2022 evidence here of Abiy's own asset filing, verification, or enforcement results."],"lenses":["7B.3","7B.6","7B.9"]}

**Search and Rejection Summary**
- I reviewed roughly 30 documents across Reuters/Euronews, CPJ, Freedom House, HRW, Access Now, The New Humanitarian, ENA, PMO, CIA, World Bank Live, policy/legal repositories, and a few local reporting and archive pages.
- I kept multiple independent reports on the same media-crackdown pattern, but I did not duplicate the same arrest story across every outlet.
- I rejected several macroeconomic, development, and general governance pieces because they lacked a direct ruler-personal-integrity nexus.
- I excluded or treated as context only older Tigray-war baseline pieces, 2026 follow-ups, and broad anti-corruption framework pages that did not show Abiy's own conduct.
- One Addis Standard anti-corruption committee page returned 403 and was unusable directly.
- I also checked asset-disclosure and corruption-framework material; it was useful for context, but I did not find a 2022 source that directly proved Abiy's own filing, verification, or personal conflict-of-interest compliance.

**Remaining Gaps**
- I did not find traceable 2022 evidence of Abiy or his close family self-enriching, holding hidden assets, using beneficial ownership structures, or receiving kickbacks.
- 7B.3 and 7B.4 remain thin: I found an asset-disclosure legal framework and anti-corruption rhetoric, but not a public, verifiable 2022 compliance trail for Abiy's own assets or conflicts.
- Appointment evidence is partial: I found a 2022 cabinet roster and one clearly technocratic finance minister biography, but not a systematic, ruler-specific record showing that Abiy avoided loyalists or cronies across the full cabinet.
- More direct evidence from FEACC filings, procurement audits, court findings, or investigative reporting on Abiy's immediate circle would materially improve confidence.
